$ enola history frobnicate
exit: 2
--- stdout
--- stderr
Usage: enola history <push|pull|verify|gc> [store_dir] [flags] [repo_path|config_path]

Share the architecture history through a directory store — a git repository, a
shared mount, an S3-synced folder. Plain files, no daemon, no database.

  push    copy local revisions into the store, and record them on this
          machine's chain
  pull    import revisions other machines pushed into the local history
  verify  walk every chain and report gaps and tampering by name
  gc      apply a retention policy to the store; prints what it would remove
          and deletes nothing without --apply

The store directory is the first argument, or `history.shared_dir` in the config.
